From fce2b43a26d4bf50832ddca2e0ac0b893d20f3ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:18:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 308/406] Assembly: a solve that does not hold puts the parts
 back and says which joint

When the joints could not be made to hold (a cylindrical joint whose
faces were 36 mm apart along the axis), solve() returned -7 and left the
parts in a broken pose (a crank 16 degrees off its bearing); the only word
was a warning in the closed report view (engine field test 0.7.3). Now
the parts go back to where they were before the solve, the warning names
the joints and how far off they are, getBrokenJoints() gives
[(joint, gap mm, angle deg)], and the design check lists "Joint does not
hold" with the distance. The check also covers cylindrical and slider
joints (off the axis) and the axes of revolute ones, with a tolerance
above the solver's convergence.

Test: FreeCADCmd -t TestAssemblySolve, -t TestAssemblyWorkbench

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
